   "daf": "37b",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "וְעַל מַשְׁקֵה בֵּי מַטְבְּחַיָּא דְּכַן. מַאי ״דְּכַן״? רַב אָמַר: דְּכַן מַמָּשׁ, וּשְׁמוּאֵל אָמַר: דְּכַן מִלְּטַמֵּא אֲחֵרִים, אֲבָל טוּמְאַת עַצְמָן יֵשׁ בָּהֶן.",
   "en": "§ It was stated above: «And» Yosei ben Yo’ezer testified «with regard to the liquids of the slaughterhouse» in the Temple that they are «ritually pure.» The Gemara asks: «What» did Yosei ben Yo’ezer mean when he said they are «pure? Rav says:» He meant that they are «actually ritually pure. And Shmuel says: They are pure» in the sense that they do not «impart ritual impurity to other» substances; «but they themselves» can contract «impurity.»"
  }
 ],
